Phase 8 verification report. Scope since the Phase 7 checkpoint 107d730: the icons (scripts/blender-icon.py + the three PNGs), the placeholder generator and its five tests removed, the Cloudflare Pages runbook plus the Workers-flow detour, README.md and LICENSE, the Blender temp-path cleanup, docs/playtest.md, and the live deployment. Gates: biome 71 files clean, tsc --noEmit clean, 361 tests across 28 files (five fewer than the previous phase - the retired placeholder suite), coverage All files 82.58 stmts.

Verified beyond the local machine, which is what this phase is for: the deployed site at https://tiny-town-explorer.pages.dev answers 200 for /, /sw.js, /manifest.webmanifest, an icon and a hashed GLB at the exact byte sizes the local production build produced; the built output was served locally and checked in a browser first, with a WebGL 2.0 context, a service worker registered at /sw.js and already controlling the page, one cache populated, six HUD buttons and the parent gear present, and an empty console.

Performance, measured rather than assumed: 37,904 triangles per frame including the shadow-map pass, across 134 draw calls and 106 meshes, against the spec's ~50k budget - so the ratchet the spec reserved has no reason to fire. Method and figures live in docs/playtest.md.

The reviewer ran the device sitting in docs/playtest.md on the iPad: loaded against the deployed URL, installed to the home screen, played offline in airplane mode, and judged the frame rate on the device. Reported all fine, which closes AC8 and the audible half of AC1 - the two criteria no desktop could answer. One fault in this phase and it was not in the game: the project was first created as a Worker, and Cloudflare's deploy step tried to install wrangler and the Vite plugin into the repo and died on the frozen lockfile with ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS. Recorded in the runbook so it is recognised next time rather than debugged.
